5. Architectural Principles

Modularity

Every component must have a defined responsibility and documented interface.

Replaceability

Model providers and infrastructure components should be replaceable without unnecessary changes to the rest of the system.

Ownership

XSUS should retain control of its original code, configurations, documentation, and eligible intellectual property.

Interoperability

Components should communicate through stable, documented interfaces.

Security by Design

Security and privacy must be considered from the earliest design stages.

Evidence-Based Development

Features must be validated through repeatable tests and measurable outcomes.

Reproducibility

Important experiments, model versions, dataset versions, and configurations should be traceable.

Incremental Scaling

Infrastructure should grow according to demonstrated demand rather than speculative requirements.

